# Architecture & Naming

## Layer Rules

```
Controller → Service → Repository → PrismaService
```

| Layer | Responsibility | May import |
|---|---|---|
| Controller | HTTP only — no business logic, no Prisma | Service |
| Service | All business logic — no Prisma | Repository, StorageService, QueueService |
| Repository | All Prisma queries — nothing else | PrismaService |

No circular dependencies. Never skip or merge layers.

## Module File Structure

```
modules/example/
├── example.module.ts
├── example.controller.ts
├── example.service.ts
├── example.repository.ts
└── dto/
    ├── create-example.dto.ts
    ├── update-example.dto.ts
    └── example-response.dto.ts
```

Every new module must include controller + service + repository.

## Naming

| Thing | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Files | kebab-case | `create-product.dto.ts` |
| Classes | PascalCase | `ProductsService` |
| Variables / functions | camelCase | `getProductById` |
| DB tables / columns | snake_case | `product_variants`, `selling_price` |
| Prisma models | PascalCase | `ProductVariant` |
| API routes | kebab-case plural | `/product-variants` |
| Env vars / queues / constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `JWT_SECRET`, `NOTIFICATION_QUEUE` |
| Booleans | is/has/can prefix | `isActive`, `hasDiscount` |
